sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Person
    participant UI as Login page (login/page.tsx)
    participant SB as Supabase Auth
    participant API as Backend API
    participant Dep as auth_deps.py

    Person->>UI: enters email + password, clicks "Sign in"
    UI->>SB: supabase.auth.signInWithPassword()
    SB-->>UI: access token (JWT)
    Note over UI: token saved in the browser<br/>(persistSession: true) — survives a page reload
    UI->>Person: redirected into the app

    Note over Person,API: later — Person asks a chat question or opens the dashboard

    UI->>API: request with header<br/>Authorization: Bearer &lt;token&gt;
    API->>Dep: get_current_user_optional()
    Dep->>SB: verify_supabase_token(token)<br/>client.auth.get_user(token)
    SB-->>Dep: user record, or an error

    alt token valid
        Dep-->>API: user dict {id, email, app_metadata.role}
    else missing / expired / invalid / Supabase unreachable
        Dep-->>API: None — never raises, request still proceeds
    end

    alt route only needs "is someone logged in?" (chat)
        API->>API: proceed either way — anonymous chat is allowed
    else route needs a specific role (admin dashboard, reindex)
        API->>Dep: require_roles(["Owner","Admin"])
        Dep->>Dep: read role from user.app_metadata.role
        alt role missing or not allowed
            Dep-->>API: 403 Forbidden
        else role allowed
            Dep-->>API: user dict — request proceeds
        end
    end

    Note over API,Dep: one more path exists for the nightly cron job:<br/>require_roles_or_automation_token() accepts a secret<br/>X-Automation-Token header instead of a login, since<br/>a scheduled job has no human session to present
